-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC # Identity and Access Architecture
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Prior to Unity Catalog, user and group management in Databricks was predominantly workspace-centric, meaning users and groups were defined and managed within the boundaries of individual workspaces. Workspace admins would manually create users and groups or synchronize them through a connected identity provider. But crucially, these identities were scoped only to the workspace in which they lived. There was no inherent synchronization across multiple workspaces, which resulted in fragmented identity management and governance challenges for organizations with complex, multi-workspace deployments.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Groups created at the workspace level were considered “workspace-local groups.” Such groups could not be assigned to other workspaces or granted access to data in any centralized way that spanned workspaces
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC This legacy model required manual effort to replicate governance structures across workspaces, complicating the implementation of consistent access, role assignment, and data management across an organization’s Databricks landscape.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC <div style="border-left: 4px solid #ff9800; background: #fff3e0; padding: 16px 20px; border-radius: 8px; margin: 16px 0;">
-- MAGIC   <div style="display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 12px;">
-- MAGIC     <span style="font-size: 24px;">⚠️</span>
