-- MAGIC %md-sandbox
-- MAGIC ### B2. Service Principals
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC A service principal is another individual entity, but one that is NOT mapped to a person. They are identified by a globally unique identifier that is generated by Databricks when the service principal is created (but they are also assigned a name to make management easier through the user interface).
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC Service principals are similar to users in many respects. Primarily, they're individual entities that are defined at account level.
-- MAGIC
-- MAGIC But unlike users, they’re based on permanent, autonomous identities. But unlike users, which may come and go, they're permanent, autonomous identities meant for running jobs, and are an excellent choice for external integrations that operate through Databricks SDKs or APIs. In this case, they authenticate using personal access tokens (PATs) or machine-to-machine (M2M).
